<p>Recently I read <a href="https://unsung.aresluna.org/i-just-chose-words-carefully/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><em>I just chose words carefully</em></a>, by Marcin Wichary, and it fascinated me. It is about building a perfect right-justified margin by hand, choosing the right words to fit them into the 79 characters the terminal imposed.</p>
<p>Then a question kept spinning in my head: if today we read on phones, what would the equivalent width be?</p>
<h2 id="blog-single-content__title--the-mobile-calculation" class="blog-single__content-title">The mobile calculation</h2>
<p>Taking the typical viewport widths in logical pixels and subtracting about 16 px of margin on each side:</p>
